From fe5563048d97e432a3931a5f8fe10b0535704a98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Macktherealonereally <macdev@mackthessd.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 13:09:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Telephony: Start SIM calls in VoIP audio mode with
 config_use_voip_mode_for_ims

With config_use_voip_mode_for_ims, ImsPhoneConnection reports VoIP
audio mode, but Telecom only learns this after the connection has been
created. Outgoing calls therefore enter MODE_IN_CALL first and switch
to MODE_IN_COMMUNICATION a few hundred milliseconds later. On Samsung
Exynos devices the audio HAL starts and stops the modem voice call path
for that transient mode, and an uplink capture stream opened meanwhile
keeps the in-call capture configuration.

Set PhoneAccount.EXTRA_ALWAYS_USE_VOIP_AUDIO_MODE on non-emergency PSTN
accounts when the overlay is enabled, so Telecom starts these calls in
MODE_IN_COMMUNICATION. Circuit-switched connections still report
non-VoIP audio mode on creation, which moves the call to MODE_IN_CALL
as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I29305d744bec55b209642d3324396f5b94fa6686
---
 .../services/telephony/TelecomAccountRegistry.java     | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/com/android/services/telephony/TelecomAccountRegistry.java b/src/com/android/services/telephony/TelecomAccountRegistry.java
index 4a90dc1..3f3f5b6 100644
--- a/src/com/android/services/telephony/TelecomAccountRegistry.java
+++ b/src/com/android/services/telephony/TelecomAccountRegistry.java
@@ -518,6 +518,16 @@ public class TelecomAccountRegistry {
                     mContext.getResources()
                             .getBoolean(R.bool.config_support_video_calling_fallback));
 
+            // Devices that run IMS media on the application processor use VoIP audio mode for
+            // IMS calls. Start calls on this account in VoIP audio mode as well, so Telecom does
+            // not set MODE_IN_CALL (which starts the modem voice path in the audio HAL) before
+            // the IMS connection reports its audio mode. Circuit-switched connections still
+            // report non-VoIP audio mode and move the call to MODE_IN_CALL.
+            if (!isEmergency && mContext.getResources().getBoolean(
+                    com.android.internal.R.bool.config_use_voip_mode_for_ims)) {
+                extras.putBoolean(PhoneAccount.EXTRA_ALWAYS_USE_VOIP_AUDIO_MODE, true);
+            }
+
             if (slotId != SubscriptionManager.INVALID_SIM_SLOT_INDEX) {
                 extras.putInt(PhoneAccount.EXTRA_SORT_ORDER, slotId);
             }
